  "structuring": {
    "prompt_additions": "Finland uses CHAPTER (luku) as the primary higher division, not PART. The basic unit is § (pykälä), rendered as SECTION. Many short acts have no chapter divisions at all — do not force a chapter wrapper. The enacting formula in Finnish is 'Eduskunnan päätöksen mukaisesti säädetään:' and in Swedish 'I enlighet med riksdagens beslut föreskrivs:'. Sections are numbered N § (number before symbol). Subsections (momentti) are numbered (1), (2), (3). Points (kohta) within subsections may be numbered 1), 2), 3) or a), b), c) — detect from context. Inserted sections use alphanumeric suffixing with a space: '5 a §' — normalise to SECTION 5a in Bluebell."
  },
